// `ColumnWidths::default()` — disassembly column geometry (px).
//
// `comment` is a *minimum*; the per-frame render stretches the comment
// area to `(window_w - left_columns_total).max(comment)` so it fills
// remaining width. `margin` (26) gives the bookmark glyph + breakpoint
// number ~12 px each. `address` (150) was bumped from 130 on 2026-04-30
// for breathing room around the hex literal.
//
// The same field set is inlined into `disasm_view/config.ron` (under
// `columns:`); drift between this file and that block is guarded by
// `tests::columns_inline_in_config_ron_matches_canonical`.

(
    margin: 26.0,
    arrows: 36.0,
    address: 150.0,
    bytes: 200.0,
    mnemonic: 80.0,
    operands: 220.0,
    comment: 100.0,
)
